        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bernhard Heiden, Paul Hindemith\n- Roles: composer, music teacher, violist, violinist, conductor\n- Places: Frankfurt-am-Main, Bloomington, Indiana\n\nFacts:\n- Paul Hindemith was born on 16 November 1895 and died on 28 December 1963.\n- Paul Hindemith was a prolific German composer, violist, violinist, teacher, and conductor.\n- Bernhard Heiden was born in Frankfurt-am-Main on August 24, 1910, and died in Bloomington, Indiana, on April 30, 2000.\n- Bernhard Heiden was a German and American composer and music teacher.\n- Bernhard Heiden studied under Paul Hindemith and was heavily influenced by him.",
